This is a React TypeScript CRM power dialer web app.
Stack: React, TypeScript, Supabase (database + edge functions),
LiveKit Cloud (WebRTC browser SDK: livekit-client) + Telnyx SIP trunk for PSTN.
Goal: Full production deployment. Fix ALL bugs, errors, and
broken logic across the entire codebase.

## Architecture

- Browser WebRTC: LiveKit Cloud rooms via `livekit-client` SDK
- PSTN calls: Telnyx SIP trunk connected to LiveKit SIP bridge (server-side only)
- Call flow: agent browser joins LiveKit room → edge fn creates outbound SIP participant → Telnyx dials the lead
- Recording: LiveKit Egress (server-side composite, audio-only OGG)

## Key files

- Dialer page: src/pages/Dialer.tsx
- Dialer queue hook: src/hooks/use-dialer-queue.ts (campaignId param, flat QueueContact shape)
- LiveKit browser hook: src/hooks/use-livekit-client.ts (dial/hangUp/toggleMute/toggleHold/sendDTMF)
- Campaign phone pool: src/hooks/use-campaign-phones.ts
- Dialer service (predictive): src/lib/dialer-service.ts
- Edge functions: supabase/functions/livekit-call-control/ (dial/hangup/transfer)
                  supabase/functions/livekit-token/ (browser JWT)
                  supabase/functions/livekit-webhook/ (room events)
                  supabase/functions/power-dialer-next/ (next lead for agent)

